1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:05,179
这是 Josh 在示例 notebook 里写下的一整个科研实验
Here is a whole research experiment, as Josh's example notebook writes it.

2
00:00:05,499 --> 00:00:08,592
只有四个调用：setup、train、predict、evaluate
Four calls: set up, train, predict, evaluate.

3
00:00:08,767 --> 00:00:10,541
它们背后是一个文件
Behind them sits one file,

4
00:00:10,541 --> 00:00:14,635
speciesot_core.py，大约三百五十行
speciesot_core.py, about three hundred and fifty lines long.

5
00:00:14,635 --> 00:00:15,932
哪些行重要？
Which lines matter,

6
00:00:15,932 --> 00:00:18,388
到底该从哪里读起？
and where do you even start reading?

7
00:00:18,567 --> 00:00:20,451
诀窍是：这个文件里的每一个类
Here's the trick: every class

8
00:00:20,451 --> 00:00:25,712
都属于五种分工之一——数据、契约、指挥、模型、指标
in that file does one of five jobs. Data, contract, conductor, model, and metric.

9
00:00:25,712 --> 00:00:27,512
我们来学会看出它们
Let's learn to see them.

10
00:00:30,367 --> 00:00:33,661
先从撑起整个文件的那个词开始：class，类
Start with the word the whole file is built from: class.

11
00:00:33,661 --> 00:00:38,309
类是一张蓝图：它描述一个东西会知道什么、能做什么
A class is a blueprint. It describes what a thing will know and what it can do,

12
00:00:38,309 --> 00:00:40,109
但它本身还不是那个东西
but it isn't the thing itself.

13
00:00:40,234 --> 00:00:43,477
像调用函数一样调用一个类，就会按蓝图造出一个对象
Calling a class like a function builds an object from it.

14
00:00:43,797 --> 00:00:49,727
第 115 行正是这么做的：scGenModel，传入属于它的那一段配置
Line 115 does exactly that: scGenModel, given its slice of the config.

15
00:00:49,900 --> 00:00:53,527
对象一造好，Python 就会运行它的 init 方法
The moment the object is built, Python runs its init method.

16
00:00:53,847 --> 00:00:57,100
init 的每一行都往新对象身上写一个事实
Each line of init writes one fact onto the new object:

17
00:00:57,100 --> 00:01:00,716
学习率、潜空间大小、模型保存在哪里
the learning rate, the latent size, where to save the model.

18
00:01:00,867 --> 00:01:03,888
self 的意思就是「这个对象自己」
And self just means this particular object.

19
00:01:03,888 --> 00:01:06,558
self.lr 就是这个模型自己的学习率
self.lr is this model's learning rate.

20
00:01:06,558 --> 00:01:09,720
造两个模型，它们各自保存各自的
Build two models, and each one keeps its own.

21
00:01:13,667 --> 00:01:17,678
文件开头附近有一种不一样的类：AbstractModel
Near the top of the file is a different kind of class: AbstractModel.

22
00:01:17,998 --> 00:01:22,115
它的每个方法都标着 abstract（抽象），方法体里只会抛出错误
Every method is marked abstract, and its body only raises an error.

23
00:01:22,267 --> 00:01:25,639
这是一份契约：任何自称「模型」的东西
It's a contract. Anything that calls itself a model

24
00:01:25,639 --> 00:01:28,548
都必须会 setup、train 和 predict
must know how to set up, train, and predict.

25
00:01:28,548 --> 00:01:32,251
契约只写下方法的名字，不负责填写内容
The contract names the methods. It doesn't fill them in.

26
00:01:32,400 --> 00:01:37,136
停下来猜一猜：如果直接去造一个 AbstractModel，会发生什么？
Pause and predict: what happens if you try to build an AbstractModel directly?

27
00:01:40,300 --> 00:01:41,829
Python 会拒绝
Python refuses.

28
00:01:41,879 --> 00:01:45,646
我们实际跑过：无法实例化抽象类 AbstractModel
We ran it: can't instantiate abstract class AbstractModel

29
00:01:45,646 --> 00:01:49,282
因为 predict、setup、train 都还没有实现
without an implementation for predict, setup and train.

30
00:01:49,434 --> 00:01:52,805
IdentityModel 和 scGenModel 把空白填上了
IdentityModel and scGenModel fill in the blanks.

31
00:01:53,125 --> 00:01:58,458
在类名后面的圆括号里写上 AbstractModel，就是它们签下契约的方式
Writing AbstractModel in parentheses after the class name is how they sign the contract.

32
00:01:58,778 --> 00:02:00,350
这叫继承
That's called inheritance.

33
00:02:00,400 --> 00:02:03,969
看 train：契约里的 train 接收训练数据
Look at train. The contract's train takes training data,

34
00:02:03,969 --> 00:02:07,920
IdentityModel 的 train 什么都不接收，可 Python 照样把它造了出来
but IdentityModel's takes nothing, and Python still builds it.

35
00:02:07,920 --> 00:02:10,342
契约只检查名字，不检查参数
The contract checks names, not inputs.

36
00:02:10,500 --> 00:02:15,193
你还会在 Experiment 和数据类上看到 abc.ABC
You'll also see abc.ABC on Experiment and the data classes.

37
00:02:15,513 --> 00:02:18,351
它们没有抽象方法，也就没有要签的条款
With no abstract methods, there's nothing to sign.

38
00:02:18,671 --> 00:02:24,708
Josh 第 19 行的注释说数据类可以去掉它，Experiment 也一样
Josh's note on line 19 says the data classes can drop it, and the same goes for Experiment.

39
00:02:27,600 --> 00:02:29,981
Experiment 类是指挥
The Experiment class is the conductor.

40
00:02:29,981 --> 00:02:36,624
它自己从不做科学计算：它读配置、造出各个部件，再告诉每个部件何时上场
It never does the science itself. It reads the config, builds the pieces, and tells each one when to play.

41
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:41,795
setup 会填好两个列表：models 来自 config.yaml 的 models 部分
Setup fills two lists: models, from the models section of config.yaml,

42
00:02:41,795 --> 00:02:45,077
evaluations 来自 evaluations 部分
and evaluations, from the evaluations section.

43
00:02:45,233 --> 00:02:47,750
train 和 predict 沿着 models 列表逐个执行
Train and predict walk down the models list.

44
00:02:48,006 --> 00:02:52,657
predict 从每个模型收集一个答案：一组预测出的人类细胞
Predict collects one answer from each model: a set of predicted human cells.

45
00:02:52,833 --> 00:02:57,889
evaluate 把两个列表交叉起来：两个模型乘以两个指标，得到四个数字
Evaluate crosses the two lists. Two models times two metrics: four numbers.

46
00:02:58,067 --> 00:02:59,425
说一个实情
One honest detail:

47
00:02:59,425 --> 00:03:04,252
按现在的写法，evaluate 算出这些数字后就把它们丢掉了
as written, evaluate computes those numbers and then drops them.

48
00:03:04,252 --> 00:03:06,289
第 145 行没有存下来
Line 145 never stores them.

49
00:03:06,289 --> 00:03:08,627
第五集会回到这一点
Remember that for episode five.

50
00:03:12,633 --> 00:03:16,537
回报在这里：第 137 行调用 model.predict
Here's the payoff. Line 137 calls model.predict,

51
00:03:16,537 --> 00:03:20,441
却从不过问自己在和哪个模型说话
without ever asking which model it's talking to.

52
00:03:20,600 --> 00:03:24,525
IdentityModel 的回答是原封不动地交回小鼠细胞
IdentityModel answers by handing back the mouse cells unchanged.

53
00:03:24,845 --> 00:03:29,752
它是「什么都不做」的基线：真正的模型至少要胜过直接照抄小鼠
It's the do-nothing baseline: a real model has to beat simply copying the mouse.

54
00:03:29,900 --> 00:03:34,390
scGenModel 则会把小鼠细胞往人类方向平移
scGenModel will answer by shifting the mouse cells toward human.

55
00:03:34,390 --> 00:03:38,177
同一个问题，不同的回答——这就是多态
Same question, different answers. That's polymorphism.

56
00:03:38,333 --> 00:03:41,762
那么想一想：当你把 CellOT 加进来作为第三个模型时
So think about it: when you add CellOT as a third model,

57
00:03:41,762 --> 00:03:44,946
Experiment 里有哪些行应该改动？
which lines of the Experiment should have to change?

58
00:03:47,566 --> 00:03:48,945
理想情况是一行都不用改
Ideally, none.

59
00:03:48,995 --> 00:03:53,433
但目前 setup 里还用一串 if 语句逐个点名模型
Today, setup still names each model by hand, in a chain of if statements.

60
00:03:53,753 --> 00:03:55,758
第五集会接着解决这个问题
Episode five pulls on that thread.

61
00:03:57,367 --> 00:04:01,570
回顾一下。类是蓝图，对象按蓝图造出来
Recap. A class is a blueprint, and an object is built from it.

62
00:04:01,890 --> 00:04:05,047
init 写下对象的事实，self 指的就是这个对象本身
Init writes the object's facts, and self means this one.

63
00:04:05,200 --> 00:04:07,273
抽象类是一份契约
An abstract class is a contract.

64
00:04:07,273 --> 00:04:13,169
它写下方法名，在每个方法都填好之前，Python 不会造出这个模型
It names the methods, and Python won't build a model until every named method is filled in.

65
00:04:13,169 --> 00:04:14,984
但它只检查名字，不检查参数
It checks names, not inputs.

66
00:04:14,984 --> 00:04:17,446
第五集会看到什么会漏过去
Episode five shows what slips through.

67
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:22,251
Experiment 负责指挥，模型和指标通过各自的契约接进来
The Experiment conducts, and models and metrics plug into it through their contracts.

68
00:04:22,400 --> 00:04:25,939
轮到你了：在这里暂停，打开 speciesot_core.py
Your turn: pause here, open speciesot_core.py,

69
00:04:25,939 --> 00:04:29,632
给每个类标上五种分工之一
and label every class with one of the five jobs.

70
00:04:29,952 --> 00:04:31,766
这张表就是你的答案
This table is your answer key.
